# Minimal curation reference host: scheduling examples.
# Replace /srv/wiki/vault and /var/lib/kb-curation with your own paths.
# Cron only schedules *deterministic* actions; the model half (understanding
# sources and proposing changes per the ingest skill) needs a separate
# scheduled Agent task that calls this host.

# Every hour: list open sources so the worker loop can pick them up.
0 * * * * /usr/bin/python3 /srv/wiki/reference-host/curation_host.py --vault /srv/wiki/vault --state /var/lib/kb-curation pending

# Daily 21:35: verify yesterday's commits (example: re-verify the latest
# commit_key recorded by your worker; never trust self-reported outputs).
35 21 * * * /usr/bin/python3 /srv/wiki/reference-host/curation_host.py --vault /srv/wiki/vault --state /var/lib/kb-curation verify --commit-key LATEST >> /var/log/kb-curation-verify.log 2>&1

# Note: "LATEST" above is a placeholder. Your worker records real commit_keys
# in its own ledger; loop over them instead of inventing this token.
